CUDA CRT 13.2.86 (CUDA Toolkit 13.2.2), Linux x86_64, nvcc + libc++ 21.
Observed failures: removed std::__promote in pow, mismatched isnan noexcept,
and classification declarations conflicting with libc++ using declarations.
Rationale/scope: enable the existing modern-libc++ math branches on Linux
with libc++ >= 21. Do not enable Android C-library branches or alter other
standard libraries, older libc++ versions or non-Linux platforms.
Verification: all 17 original autoware_cuda_utils GPU cases passed with
CUDA 13.2.2/nvcc, hermetic LLVM/libc++ 21.1.8 and sm_120 (2026-11-18).
The native full-core startup/behavior/shutdown regression also passed.
Upstream status: local compatibility experiment; CUDA 13.2 rejects libc++ on
x86 by policy. No upstream fix or vendor support is claimed.

